    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "dots1",
        "title": "Dots1 assembly and runtime contracts",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Registration makes Config.from_directory select Dots1Config. It accepts explicit head_dim or derives hidden_size // num_attention_heads, defaults KV heads to query heads, and requires supplied activation/scoring settings to be silu, noaux_tc and normalized top-k probabilities. Dense and expert widths are required. Defaults are one shared expert, 128 routed experts, eight selected experts, three initial dense layers and routed scale 2.5.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_4c535927b72f4ea4a2b1ff52c8a9e7f4",
              "call_e2114d9afaa94e66835167b308aa38fe",
              "call_d86790bf973d49678cfbd03d76bffd19"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "dots-studio/dots.llm1.base specifies hidden size 4096, 32 query/KV heads, 62 layers, dense width 10944, expert width 1408, 128 routed experts, six selected experts, two shared experts and one initial dense layer. dots-studio/dots.llm1.inst independently specifies the same values. Both omit head_dim, use RMS epsilon 1e-5, untied embeddings, vocabulary 152064, rope_theta 10000000 and position limit 32768. Their counts override the differing builder defaults. Base EOS is 151643; instruction EOS is 151645.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_17e4a2ef49fe447cb1bd0dddb963948f",
              "call_6641bee795a04cba95a463ad14925aaa",
              "call_e2114d9afaa94e66835167b308aa38fe"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Integer calculations give head dimension 128, attention width 4096, shared width 2816, one dense block and 61 sparse blocks. Rounding dense width to a 128-element multiple gives 11008. These are transcribed shape calculations, not tensor tests.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_449c0ff815694de282c6c2388b45453f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The pipeline is embedding \u2192 sequential pre-normalized TransformerBlocks \u2192 final RMSNorm \u2192 vocabulary Linear. Each block adds attention, then normalizes the updated residual before its MLP. Q/K normalization operates per head before RoPE; V is not normalized. The builder selects NEOX RoPE, unspecified attention scale and no sliding window. Attention/MLP outputs request FP32; gated intermediates and final normalization request FP16.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_e2114d9afaa94e66835167b308aa38fe",
              "call_247054539f9d4ff1b4e7edc49af417c7",
              "call_812388b25d714a3484046a696a90e091",
              "call_d86790bf973d49678cfbd03d76bffd19"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "idx < first_k_dense_replace selects GatedMLP; later blocks combine BlockSparseMLP with a shared GatedMLP of width moe_intermediate_size \u00d7 n_shared_experts. Each expert computes down(silu(gate(x)) \u00d7 up(x)). Routed outputs are weighted and accumulated, then shared output is added without routing weights. GatedMLP supplies the projection lists required by shared-expert allocation, avoiding the inherited plain-MLP interface mismatch.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_e2114d9afaa94e66835167b308aa38fe",
              "call_52db8331983c45d18ee119810b923a34",
              "call_10e518f8915d4aeeae77b6698963521b",
              "call_247054539f9d4ff1b4e7edc49af417c7"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "deepseekv3_routing=True and n_group=topk_group=1 select routing_dots. It adds correction bias to logits, selects top-k, applies sigmoid, normalizes with a 1e-20 stabilizer and scales by routed_scaling_factor. Thus 2.5 scales the mixture; the two ones satisfy dispatch prerequisites. Unlike routing_ds3, bias affects weights as well as selection. The builder supplies scaling, and the sampled checkpoint supplies gate.e_score_correction_bias.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_e2114d9afaa94e66835167b308aa38fe",
              "call_52db8331983c45d18ee119810b923a34",
              "call_8a62af66837e4675b221b577569502c0"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Multiple flattened tokens or non-EXL3 experts use ordinary grouping. One token with fully EXL3 experts uses indexed multi-GEMM. MultiLinear requires matching dimensions, bit widths and decoder multipliers, absent biases/softcaps and unit post-scale. Dots avoids the ancestor's default native-call mismatch and unassigned grouped-route case, but leaves the conditional all-expert buffer mismatch unchanged.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_e2114d9afaa94e66835167b308aa38fe",
              "call_52db8331983c45d18ee119810b923a34",
              "call_66bb31ddabdf4825b01e7b5a0a92d9d9",
              "call_a42c248d9f474413bd5d4564ed311829"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Base checkpoint samples contain embedding/head [152064,4096], attention matrices [4096,4096], Q/K norms [128], residual norms [4096], dense gate/up [10944,4096] and down [4096,10944]. Sparse samples contain expert gate/up [1408,4096], down [4096,1408], router [128,4096], correction bias [128], shared gate/up [2816,4096] and down [4096,2816]. model.norm.weight is [4096]. All sampled tensors are BF16.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_327b3cbb738c4f2090a1c2f5e8deca33",
              "call_8a62af66837e4675b221b577569502c0",
              "call_81c7b1ec0f894c8bb04cafac055db107"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Linear checks EXL3 groups before requesting ordinary .weight with float2half=True and transposition. It also requests optional .bias and .weight_scale_inv; EXL3 loading requests trellis and optional scale, rotation and multiplier tensors. The builder configures no fused-QKV alternative. Samples support ordinary naming and orientation, not completeness of every optional or alternate path.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_b4bc9423264b4900b9656399ddc15d40",
              "call_e2114d9afaa94e66835167b308aa38fe",
              "call_327b3cbb738c4f2090a1c2f5e8deca33",
              "call_8a62af66837e4675b221b577569502c0"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The builder clears the first attention o_proj's qmap, with a comment reporting irregularity that breaks quantization. It also enables calibration_all_experts: conversion passes that flag during capture and recomputes reference states using ordinary selected-expert routing. These settings affect calibration rather than changing ordinary inference routing.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_e2114d9afaa94e66835167b308aa38fe",
              "call_e2040489302f4337909cd117b4dbde4a"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "prepare_inputs stores input_ids and calls prepare_for_attn, matching all twelve located callers without dropping their caller-side guards. The helper defaults to uncached FlashAttention and retains cached-mode requirements. Both references disable embedding tying, so the optional head fallback is inactive.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_e2114d9afaa94e66835167b308aa38fe",
              "call_b73ccd7416c948d99c6b516cdc6a4fa9",
              "call_e2040489302f4337909cd117b4dbde4a",
              "call_812388b25d714a3484046a696a90e091",
              "call_17e4a2ef49fe447cb1bd0dddb963948f",
              "call_6641bee795a04cba95a463ad14925aaa"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
